# Day 5: Retak (spec §2, beat plan last-seen-m3.md §3 to §5). The route split: the Harbor route follows Pak Karta's
# boat, the Network route the people who knew. Bad end #8 Wrong Name lives on the Network route.

@conversation d5_morning chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Retak" title.en="Cracks" checkpoint
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_living_day.webp music=bgm_quiet_house.mp3 ambience=amb_kampung_day.mp3 day=5 time=07:30 textbox=nvl

narration
  id: Hari 5. Senin. Seminggu persis sejak Sekar pamit ke Dinda.
  en: Day 5. Monday. Exactly a week since Sekar said goodbye to Dinda.
narration
  id: Foto subuh itu masih kebuka di HP Sekar waktu gue bangun. Dermaga kayu, bakau, kapal biru-putih. "Masih di sana."
  en: The dawn photo is still open on Sekar's phone when I wake up. A wooden jetty, mangroves, a blue and white boat. "Still there."

stage
  textbox adv
  show raka:neutral left
  show dinda:neutral right

dinda:neutral [right]
  id: Gue nggak ke kampus. Udah izin ke dosen. Bilangnya sakit.
  en: I'm not going to campus. I told my lecturer I'm sick.
dinda:neutral [if yusuf_knows_didit == true]
  id: Pak Yusuf juga nelpon tadi pagi. Katanya ada polisi yang lewat depan gang tiap dua jam. Gue nggak tahu harus lega atau tambah takut.
  en: Inspector Yusuf called this morning too. He says a patrol will come past the alley every two hours. I don't know if I should feel relieved or more scared.
dinda:angry [if threatened_bima == true]
  id: Dan Bima nggak ke polisi. Satu hari yang dia minta udah lewat. Gue cek ke Pak Yusuf, nggak ada laporan apa-apa.
  en: And Bima didn't go to the police. The one day he asked for is up. I checked with Inspector Yusuf, there's no statement from him.
dinda:neutral [if bima_leak_planted == true]
  id: Bima ngechat gue jam dua pagi. "Bilang ke Raka, gue mau ngomong. Yang bener." Abis itu dia hapus.
  en: Bima texted me at two in the morning. "Tell Raka I want to talk. Properly." Then he deleted it.

dinda:neutral
  id: Jadi. Semalem kita bilang ke mana dulu?
  en: So. Where did we say we'd start last night?

set
  set route = route_lean

raka:determined [if route == 'harbor']
  id: Dermaga. Kapal Pak Karta. Kalau Pak Hendra nggak mau ngomong, gue cari orang yang dulu pegang kapal itu.
  en: The pier. Pak Karta's boat. If Pak Hendra won't talk, I'll find the man who used to own it.
raka:determined [if route != 'harbor']
  id: Orang-orangnya. Tasya janji dateng. Dan Bima belum selesai ngomong.
  en: The people. Tasya promised to come by. And Bima isn't done talking.

branch
  if route == 'harbor' -> d5h_pier
  -> d5n_warung


@conversation d5h_pier chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Kapal Pak Karta" title.en="Pak Karta's Boat"
@scene VN bg=bg_pier_day.webp music=bgm_unease.mp3 ambience=amb_harbor_day.mp3 day=5 time=08:40

stage
  show raka:neutral left

narration
  id: Tempat Sri Rejeki biasanya bersandar kosong. Cuma ban bekasnya yang ketinggalan, masih diiket ke tiang, ngambang sendirian.
  en: The Sri Rejeki's berth is empty. Only its old tire is left, still tied to the post, floating on its own.
narration
  id: Di warung kopi, dua laki-laki pake kaos polo biru dongker lagi ngobrol sama bapak pemilik warung. Di dada kaosnya ada logo kecil. Ombak di bawah matahari terbit. "BPM".
  en: At the coffee stall, two men in navy polo shirts are talking to the owner. There's a small logo on their chests. A wave under a rising sun. "BPM".
raka:worried
  id: Bentang Pesisir Makmur.
  en: Bentang Pesisir Makmur.

choice WATCH_MEN by=raka:worried silent
  id: Mereka belum lihat lo.
  en: They haven't seen you yet.
? Duduk di ujung bangku warung, pura-pura main HP, dengerin. | Sit at the end of the stall's bench, pretend to look at your phone, listen.
  value watch
  set saw_bentang_men true
? Pergi sebelum mereka nengok. | Leave before they turn around.
  value leave

narration [if WATCH_MEN == 'watch']
  id: "Sri Rejeki baliknya jam berapa, Pak?" tanya yang lebih tinggi. "Senin malem minggu lalu, ada yang naik nggak? Cewek, pake headphone?"
  en: "What time does the Sri Rejeki come back?" asks the taller one. "Monday night last week, did anyone go out on it? A girl, with headphones?"
narration [if WATCH_MEN == 'watch']
  id: Bapak warung ngelap gelas lama banget. "Kapal mah banyak, Pak. Cewek juga banyak."
  en: The stall owner takes a long time wiping a glass. "Lots of boats, sir. Lots of girls too."
narration [if WATCH_MEN == 'watch']
  id: Yang pendek nengok ke gue. Lama. Bapak warung naruh kopi di depan gue tanpa gue pesen. "Ponakan saya. Kerjanya main HP doang." Mereka ketawa. Gue juga, telat sedetik.
  en: The shorter one looks at me. A long look. The owner sets a coffee in front of me that I never ordered. "My nephew. All he does is play on his phone." They laugh. So do I, a second too late.
narration [if WATCH_MEN == 'leave']
  id: Gue muter lewat belakang krat-krat ikan. Bau amisnya nempel lagi di baju. Kali ini gue bersyukur.
  en: I go the long way round, behind the fish crates. The smell gets into my clothes again. This time I'm grateful for it.

narration [if wulan_knows_karta == true]
  id: Tadi pagi Bu Wulan nyelipin kertas ke tangan gue di pintu. Bekas struk belanja. Di baliknya, tulisan tangannya. "Pak Karta. Gg. Kerapu 3, Kamal Muara. Rumah cat kuning."
  en: This morning Mrs. Wulan slipped a piece of paper into my hand at the door. An old shopping receipt. On the back, in her handwriting. "Pak Karta. Gg. Kerapu 3, Kamal Muara. Yellow house."
narration [if wulan_knows_karta != true]
  id: Bu Rohmah, ibu pengupas kerang, ngasih tahu alamatnya sambil tetep ngupas. "Kamal Muara. Gang Kerapu, yang catnya kuning. Bilang aja dari saya."
  en: Bu Rohmah, the mussel woman, gives me the address without stopping her shelling. "Kamal Muara. Gang Kerapu, the yellow house. Tell them I sent you."

-> d5h_karta


@conversation d5h_karta chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Pak Karta" title.en="Pak Karta"
@scene VN bg=bg_karta_house_day.webp music=bgm_low_tide.mp3 ambience=amb_kampung_day.mp3 day=5 time=10:05

stage
  show raka:neutral left

narration
  id: Yang buka pintu perempuan umur tiga puluhan, anaknya Pak Karta. Namanya Mbak Yanti. Dia ngelihat gue dari kepala sampai sepatu, terus minggir.
  en: The door is opened by a woman in her thirties, Pak Karta's daughter. Her name is Yanti. She looks me over from head to shoes, then steps aside.
narration
  id: Pak Karta berbaring di dipan kayu deket jendela. Setengah mukanya turun, kayak lilin yang meleleh di satu sisi. Tangan kirinya diem di atas selimut batik. Tangan kanannya masih kuat, megangin pinggiran dipan.
  en: Pak Karta lies on a wooden bed by the window. Half his face has fallen, like a candle melted on one side. His left hand lies still on the batik blanket. His right hand is still strong, gripping the edge of the bed.
narration
  id: Dia ngelihat gue lama. Terus mulut yang setengah itu gerak.
  en: He looks at me for a long time. Then the half of his mouth that works begins to move.

karta [offstage]
  id: Anak...{w=600} jam lima.
  en: The boy...{w=600} five o'clock.

narration
  id: Setahun. Orang yang cuma sekali denger cerita soal gue, masih inget gue sebagai orang yang nggak dateng.
  en: A year. A man who heard about me once still remembers me as the one who didn't show up.

choice TALK_KARTA by=raka:sad
  id: Apa yang lo bilang?
  en: What do you say?
? "Maaf saya nggak dateng, Pak. Waktu itu." | "I'm sorry I didn't come, sir. That day."
  value sorry
  +trust_hendra 2
? "Pak, saya nyari Sekar. Bapak tahu dia di mana?" | "Sir, I'm looking for Sekar. Do you know where she is?"
  value direct
? (Duduk di bangku plastik. Nunggu dia ngomong.) | (Sit on the plastic stool. Wait for him to speak.) [silent]
  value wait
  +trust_hendra 1

karta [offstage] [if TALK_KARTA == 'sorry']
  id: Dia...{w=500} nunggu kamu.{w=500} Terus...{w=500} tetep naik.{w=600} Anak itu...{w=400} keras kepala.
  en: She...{w=500} waited for you.{w=500} Then...{w=500} came aboard anyway.{w=600} That girl...{w=400} stubborn.
karta [offstage] [if TALK_KARTA == 'direct']
  id: Jangan...{w=600} keras-keras.
  en: Not...{w=600} so loud.
narration [if TALK_KARTA == 'direct']
  id: Matanya ngelirik ke pintu, ke jalan gang. Mbak Yanti nutup gordennya tanpa disuruh.
  en: His eyes flick to the door, to the alley. Yanti draws the curtain without being asked.
narration [if TALK_KARTA == 'wait']
  id: Gue duduk. Kipas angin muter. Di luar ada yang jualan sayur pake pengeras suara. Lima menit, mungkin lebih.
  en: I sit. The fan turns. Outside someone is selling vegetables through a loudspeaker. Five minutes, maybe more.

narration
  id: Tangan kanannya terangkat, gemeteran, nunjuk ke jendela. Ke buku bersampul kain yang udah lusuh di kusennya.
  en: His right hand rises, trembling, and points at the window. At a worn cloth-bound book on the sill.
karta [offstage]
  id: Hendra...{w=500} tulis di buku saya.{w=600} Biar saya...{w=500} tahu...{w=500} kapal saya ke mana.
  en: Hendra...{w=500} writes in my book.{w=600} So I...{w=500} know...{w=500} where my boat goes.

narration
  id: Buku log kapal. Halaman-halaman awalnya tulisan Pak Karta, miring dan rapi. Belakangan, tulisan lain, lebih tegas. Tanggal, jam, tujuan, jumlah orang.
  en: A boat's logbook. The early pages are in Pak Karta's hand, slanted and neat. Later, another hand, firmer. Date, time, destination, number of people.
narration
  id: Senin malem nggak ada catatan apa-apa. Apa pun yang terjadi di laut malam itu, Pak Hendra nggak nulisnya.
  en: Monday night has no entry at all. Whatever happened at sea that night, Pak Hendra didn't write it down.
narration
  id: Selasa. "05.30. Pari. 1 org (S.)." Digaris bawahi sekali.
  en: Tuesday. "05:30. Pari. 1 person (S.)." Underlined once.
set
  clue crossing_log
  remember knows_crossing_log

raka:shocked
  id: Pulau Pari. Jam setengah enam.
  en: Pulau Pari. Five thirty.
narration
  id: Jadwal di papan gabus Sekar. Dilingkarin dua kali. Bukan kapal penumpang. Kapal ini.
  en: The schedule on Sekar's corkboard. Circled twice. Not the passenger ferry. This boat.

karta [offstage]
  id: Jangan...{w=600} bawa orang...{w=500} ke pulau.
  en: Don't...{w=600} bring anyone...{w=500} to the island.
narration
  id: Tangan kanannya megang pergelangan gue. Kuat, lebih kuat dari yang gue kira.
  en: His right hand grips my wrist. Strong, stronger than I expected.
karta [offstage]
  id: Kamu...{w=500} jangan telat...{w=500} lagi.
  en: Don't...{w=500} be late...{w=500} again.

narration
  id: Gue motret halamannya dan naruh bukunya balik di kusen, persis di tempatnya. Mbak Yanti nganter gue sampai pintu. "Om Hendra pulang siang," katanya. "Jangan bikin dia marah. Dia lagi capek jagain banyak orang."
  en: I photograph the page and put the book back on the sill, exactly where it was. Yanti walks me to the door. "Uncle Hendra comes back at noon," she says. "Don't make him angry. He's tired of looking after so many people."

-> d5h_hendra


@conversation d5h_hendra chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Malam Senin" title.en="Monday Night"
@scene VN bg=bg_pier_day.webp music=bgm_unease.mp3 ambience=amb_harbor_day.mp3 day=5 time=12:40

stage
  show raka:neutral left

narration
  id: Sri Rejeki masuk dermaga jam satu kurang dua puluh. Mesinnya batuk dua kali sebelum mati. Orang-orang BPM udah pergi.
  en: The Sri Rejeki comes in at twenty to one. Its engine coughs twice before it dies. The BPM men are gone.

stage
  show hendra:gruff right transition=fade duration=700

hendra:gruff [right]
  id: Yanti nelpon saya. Kamu ke rumah abang saya.
  en: Yanti called me. You went to my brother's house.
raka:neutral [left]
  id: Pak Karta yang nunjukin bukunya.
  en: Pak Karta showed me the book himself.
hendra:wary
  id: Abang saya sakit. Dia nggak ngerti apa yang dia tunjukin.
  en: My brother is sick. He doesn't understand what he's showing.

evidence WHERE_SEKAR by=hendra:wary retries=1 label=where_sekar
  id: "Terus kamu mau apa?" Tunjukkan kalau lo udah tahu ke mana dia.
  en: "So what do you want?" Show him you already know where she went.
? crossing_log
  +trust_hendra 3
  -> #hendra_tells
? sunrise_photo
  +trust_hendra 3
  -> #hendra_tells
? [retry]
  -trust_hendra 1
  -> #where_retry
? [fallback]
  -trust_hendra 2
  -> #hendra_refuses

hendra:gruff label=where_retry
  id: Itu nggak ngejawab apa-apa.
  en: That doesn't answer anything.
-> #where_sekar

hendra:gruff label=hendra_refuses
  id: Saya nggak punya urusan sama kamu. Pulang.
  en: I've got no business with you. Go home.
narration
  id: Dia naik lagi ke kapalnya dan mulai ngegulung tali, punggungnya ke gue. Gue nunggu sepuluh menit. Punggungnya nggak pernah balik.
  en: He climbs back onto his boat and starts coiling rope, his back to me. I wait ten minutes. His back never turns.
set
  set hendra_refused true
-> d5h_yusuf

narration label=hendra_tells
  id: Pak Hendra ngelihat layar HP gue lama. Terus dia duduk di ember terbaliknya, kayak orang yang akhirnya naruh barang berat.
  en: Pak Hendra looks at my screen for a long time. Then he sits on his upturned bucket, like a man finally setting down something heavy.
hendra:neutral
  id: Senin malem dia dateng jam sepuluh kurang. Bawa tas sama alat rekamnya. Ada satu orang lagi yang udah nunggu di kapal. Orang kantor.
  en: Monday night she came at a little before ten. With her bag and her recording gear. There was someone else already waiting on the boat. An office man.
hendra:neutral [if trust_hendra >= 5]
  id: Pak Darmawan. Orang dinas lingkungan, yang dulu ngukur-ngukur laut buat izin itu. Dia nggak mau ngomong di darat. Katanya di darat banyak kuping.
  en: Pak Darmawan. From the city environment office, the one who did the sea surveys for that permit. He wouldn't talk on land. He said the land has too many ears.
set [if trust_hendra >= 5]
  set knows_source true
hendra:neutral [if trust_hendra < 5]
  id: Namanya nggak usah kamu tahu. Dia nggak mau ngomong di darat. Katanya di darat banyak kuping.
  en: You don't need his name. He wouldn't talk on land. He said the land has too many ears.
hendra:neutral
  id: Saya bawa mereka keluar, lewat patok. Satu jam dia ngomong ke alat rekam anak itu. Saya di buritan, nggak dengerin. Tapi saya denger.
  en: I took them out, past the stakes. He talked into her recorder for an hour. I was at the stern, not listening. But I heard.
hendra:worried
  id: Pulangnya jam setengah sebelas, di dermaga ada dua orang pake senter. Kaosnya sama kayak yang tadi pagi nanya-nanya ke warung.
  en: We came back at half past ten, and there were two men on the pier with flashlights. The same shirts as the ones asking at the stall this morning.
hendra:worried
  id: Anak itu langsung matiin HP-nya. Dia bilang, "Pak, HP bisa dicari." Saya nggak ngerti apa-apa soal HP. Saya cuma ngerti dia takut.
  en: She switched her phone off right away. She said, "Sir, phones can be tracked." I don't know anything about phones. I just knew she was scared.
raka:worried
  id: "HP bisa dicari." Bapak bilang itu ke saya tiga hari lalu.
  en: "Phones can be tracked." You said that to me three days ago.
hendra:neutral
  id: Itu kata dia. Saya cuma ngulang.
  en: Those were her words. I was only repeating them.
hendra:neutral
  id: Saya tahan kapal di tengah sampai orang-orang itu pergi. Subuh, saya bawa dia ke Pari. Ke rumah sepupu saya. Dia aman. Dia nggak mau pulang sebelum rekamannya aman.
  en: I kept the boat out until those men left. At dawn, I took her to Pari. To my cousin's house. She's safe. She won't come back until the recording is safe.
hendra:kind
  id: Foto kemarin subuh itu, dia yang minta saya kirim. Dan telepon tanpa suara itu. Dia bilang, "Raka bakal ngerti."
  en: That photo yesterday at dawn, she asked me to send it. And the call with no voice. She said, "Raka will understand."
raka:sad
  id: Gue ngerti.
  en: I understood.
set
  set hendra_told true

-> d5h_yusuf


@conversation d5h_yusuf chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Laporan" title.en="The Report"
@scene CALL channel=thread_yusuf day=5 time=15:10 bg=bg_pier_day.webp music=bgm_tense_call.mp3 ring=sfx_phone_ring.mp3 stay="Itu Ipda Yusuf. Dia nggak bakal nelpon siang-siang kalau nggak ada apa-apa." stay.en="It's Inspector Yusuf. He wouldn't call in the middle of the afternoon for nothing."

yusuf voice=vo_d5_yusuf_01.mp3
  id: Mas Raka. Ada perkembangan, dan saya rasa Anda harus dengar dari saya duluan.
  en: Mr. Raka. There's been a development, and I think you should hear it from me first.
  delivery: formal, careful, a little uneasy
yusuf voice=vo_d5_yusuf_02.mp3
  id: PT Bentang Pesisir Makmur melapor tadi siang. Mereka bilang seorang nelayan, Hendra, diduga membawa Mbak Sekar pergi. Ada saksi yang melihat Mbak Sekar naik kapalnya.
  en: PT Bentang Pesisir Makmur filed a report at noon. They say a fisherman, Hendra, is suspected of taking Ms. Sekar away. They have a witness who saw her board his boat.
  delivery: reading from a report, distaste under the formality
yusuf voice=vo_d5_yusuf_03.mp3
  id: Besok pagi ada tim ke Pulau Pari. Polisi, sama petugas "pengamanan" dari pihak pelapor. Saya keberatan dengan cara ini.
  en: Tomorrow morning a team goes to Pulau Pari. Police, and "security" from the complainant's side. That isn't a procedure I like.
  delivery: dry, the quotation marks audible
yusuf voice=vo_d5_yusuf_04.mp3 [if yusuf_knows_didit == true]
  id: Saya sudah minta masuk tim. Setelah rekaman ancaman yang Anda laporkan, saya bisa menahan keberangkatannya sampai siang. Tidak lebih.
  en: I've asked to be on the team. After the threat you reported, I can hold the departure until noon. No later.
  delivery: quiet, an ally speaking carefully on an office phone
yusuf voice=vo_d5_yusuf_05.mp3 [if yusuf_knows_didit != true]
  id: Saya tidak bisa menahan apa-apa, Mas. Saran saya, jauhi Pulau Pari. Jangan sampai Anda ikut terseret.
  en: I can't hold anything back. My advice is to stay away from Pulau Pari. Don't get yourself dragged into this.
  delivery: tired, honest about his limits
yusuf voice=vo_d5_yusuf_06.mp3 [if yusuf_knows_boat == true]
  id: Satu lagi. Nama kapal itu saya dapat dari Anda dan sudah saya catat tiga hari lalu. Sekarang pihak Bentang juga tahu namanya. Saya tidak tahu mereka dapat dari mana.
  en: One more thing. I wrote that boat's name down three days ago, from you. Now Bentang knows it as well as I do. I don't know how.
  delivery: troubled, half to himself

system
  id: Panggilan berakhir
  en: Call ended
set
  set pari_raid true

-> d5h_night


@conversation d5h_night chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Angin" title.en="Wind"
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_room_night.webp music=bgm_low_tide.mp3 ambience=amb_room_night.mp3 day=5 time=21:20

stage
  show raka:neutral left
  show dinda:neutral right

narration
  id: Malem. Angin mulai bunyi di seng-seng atap. Jendela kamar Sekar getar tiap kali ada yang lebih kenceng.
  en: Night. The wind has started to rattle the tin roofs. The window of Sekar's room shakes every time a gust comes through.
dinda:angry
  id: Bentang yang lapor Pak Hendra nyulik? Mereka yang ngancem kita, terus mereka yang lapor?
  en: Bentang reported Pak Hendra for kidnapping? They're the ones threatening us, and they're the ones reporting?
raka:neutral
  id: Kalau polisi yang dateng ke Pari, Sekar nggak bisa nolak ikut. Dan kalau orang Bentang ikut, alat rekamnya...
  en: If it's the police who come to Pari, Sekar can't refuse to go with them. And if Bentang's people are with them, her recorder...
dinda:neutral
  id: Kita harus sampai duluan.
  en: We have to get there first.

stage
  sound sfx_phone_ring.mp3

narration
  id: HP gue bunyi. Nomor yang nggak gue simpen. Suara di seberang berat, pendek-pendek, ditutupin angin.
  en: My phone rings. A number I haven't saved. The voice on the other end is heavy, clipped, half drowned by the wind.
hendra [offstage] [if hendra_refused != true]
  id: Besok angin besar. Syahbandar pasti nutup laut. Siang ada reda sebentar. Saya jalan pas reda. Satu kali, nggak nunggu.
  en: Big wind tomorrow. The harbor master will close the sea. There's a lull around midday. I go in the lull. Once, no waiting.
hendra [offstage] [if hendra_refused == true]
  id: Yanti cerita kamu duduk lima menit nungguin abang saya ngomong. Besok siang ada reda sebentar. Saya jalan pas reda. Kalau kamu ada di dermaga, kamu ikut.
  en: Yanti says you sat five minutes waiting for my brother to speak. There's a lull around midday tomorrow. I go in the lull. If you're on the pier, you come.
hendra [offstage]
  id: Jangan bawa HP anak itu.
  en: Don't bring that girl's phone.

dinda:neutral
  id: Gue ikut.
  en: I'm coming.
raka:neutral
  id: Din. Didit tahu semester lo. Kalau dua-duanya pergi, Ibu sendirian, dan HP ini...
  en: Din. Didit knows your semester. If we both go, your mom's alone, and this phone...
dinda:angry
  id: Jangan suruh gue jadi orang yang nunggu di rumah lagi, Ka.
  en: Don't make me the one who waits at home again, Ka.

choice LEAVE_PHONE by=dinda:angry
  id: HP Sekar ada di meja di antara kalian.
  en: Sekar's phone is on the desk between you.
? "Lo pegang HP-nya. Itu bukan nunggu. Itu jagain buktinya." | "You keep the phone. That's not waiting. That's guarding the evidence."
  value leave
  set left_phone true
  +trust_dinda 2
? "Gue bawa HP-nya. Kalau Sekar nelpon lagi, gue harus angkat." | "I'm taking the phone. If Sekar calls again, I have to answer."
  value take

dinda:neutral [if LEAVE_PHONE == 'leave']
  id: ...Oke. Tapi lo telepon gue tiap jam. Dari HP lo sendiri.
  en: ...Okay. But you call me every hour. From your own phone.
dinda:hopeful [if LEAVE_PHONE == 'leave']
  id: Dan bawa dia pulang.
  en: And bring her home.
dinda:angry [if LEAVE_PHONE == 'take']
  id: Pak Hendra bilang jangan. Kak Sekar bilang jangan. Lo selalu harus belajar sendiri, ya.
  en: Pak Hendra said don't. Sekar said don't. You always have to learn things the hard way, huh.

narration
  id: Gue tidur di lantai kamar Sekar, dengerin angin. Jam lima pagi, gue kebangun sendiri, tanpa alarm.
  en: I sleep on the floor of Sekar's room, listening to the wind. At five in the morning, I wake on my own, without an alarm.

-> d6h_dawn


