  -> #leak_tasya
? [fallback]
  -> #leak_vague

raka:determined label=leak_bima [if WHO_LEAKED == 'didit_card']
  id: "Nomor ini saya dapat dari Mas Bima." Kartu namanya Didit, Bim. Lo kenal dia. Lo ngasih dia nomor HP Sekar.
  en: "I got this number from Bima." That's Didit's card, Bim. You know him. You gave him Sekar's number.
raka:determined [if WHO_LEAKED == 'bima_deleted']
  id: Lo hapus pesan jam delapan empat puluh karena kantor lo nyuruh jauhin Sekar. Kenapa kantor konsultan peduli sama podcaster, Bim?
  en: You deleted that message at eight forty because your office told you to stay away from Sekar. Why would a consulting firm care about a podcaster, Bim?
narration
  id: Bima nyender ke pagar. Jam tangannya yang mahal kena lampu jalan, dan untuk pertama kalinya kelihatan kayak barang yang kebesaran buat tangannya.
  en: Bima leans against the gate. His expensive watch catches the streetlight, and for the first time it looks too big for his wrist.
bima:ashamed
  id: Gue cerita ke bos gue. Pak Rudy. Tiga minggu lalu. Gue bilang Sekar lagi bikin episode soal izin reklamasi, dan dia pegang AMDAL yang asli.
  en: I told my boss. Pak Rudy. Three weeks ago. I said Sekar was making an episode about the reclamation permit, and that she had the real environmental review.
bima:ashamed
  id: Gue pikir kalau kantor tahu, mereka bakal bilang ke klien buat hati-hati, buat beresin izinnya. Gue pikir itu bakal ngelindungin dia.
  en: I thought if the office knew, they'd tell the client to be careful, to fix the permit. I thought it would protect her.
bima:panicked
  id: Malemnya Pak Rudy email Didit. Gue di-CC. Begitu baca, gue langsung sadar. Udah telanjur.
  en: That night Pak Rudy emailed Didit. He copied me in. I read it, and I knew I'd done something I couldn't undo.
narration
  id: Dia ngeluarin HP-nya, ngetik sesuatu, dan HP gue geter. Email. Diteruskan.
  en: He takes out his phone, types something, and my phone buzzes. An email. Forwarded.
media IMAGE photo_bima_email.webp unlock=photo_bima_email
  id: "Pak Didit, info dari Bima (tim kami): Sekar A. pegang salinan AMDAL asli + rekaman orang dinas. Mohon ditangani dengan bijak."
  en: "Pak Didit, info from Bima (on our team): Sekar A. has a copy of the original AMDAL + a recording of someone from the office. Please handle it wisely."
set
  clue bima_email
  remember knows_bima_email
dinda:crying
  id: "Ditangani dengan bijak."
  en: "Handle it wisely."
bima:ashamed
  id: Senin sore Sekar nanya ke gue jadwal kapal ke Pulau Pari. Gue kira buat liputan. Gue nggak nanya. Gue nggak pernah nanya apa-apa ke dia.
  en: Monday afternoon Sekar asked me about the ferry times to Pulau Pari. I thought it was for a story. I didn't ask. I never asked her anything.
set
  set bima_confessed true
-> d5n_night

# Dinda stops a wrong accusation once, if she trusts Raka enough to argue. Otherwise, or the second time, Raka names Tasya.
branch label=leak_tasya
  if trust_dinda >= 10 && dinda_stopped_wrong != true -> #dinda_stops
  -> d5n_wrong_name

dinda:angry label=dinda_stops
  id: Bukan Tasya, Ka. Halaman itu bilang dia bukan jahat. Dan Didit sendiri yang bilang ke Tasya dia udah denger dari orang lain.
  en: It isn't Tasya, Ka. That page says she isn't bad. And Didit told Tasya himself that he'd already heard from someone else.
set
  set dinda_stopped_wrong true
  -trust_dinda 2
-> #who_leaked

bima:irritated label=leak_vague
  id: Itu nggak ngebuktiin apa-apa, Ka. Gue capek dicurigain.
  en: That doesn't prove anything, Ka. I'm tired of being suspected.
narration
  id: Dia balik ke mobilnya. Lampu belakangnya merah, terus belok, terus hilang. Kayak semua orang di cerita ini.
  en: He walks back to his car. Its tail lights are red, then they turn, then they're gone. Like everyone in this story.
-> d5n_night


@conversation d5n_wrong_name chapter="Hari 5" chapter.en="Day 5" title="Nama yang Salah" title.en="Wrong Name"
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_room_night.webp music=bgm_low_tide.mp3 day=5 time=21:30

narration
  id: Malem itu gue buka grup pendengar dari HP Sekar. Jari gue gemeteran, tapi bukan karena ragu.
  en: That night I open the listener group on Sekar's phone. My fingers shake, but not from doubt.
narration
  id: "Ini Raka, temennya Sekar. Tasya tahu Sekar diancam seminggu sebelum dia hilang, dan diem. Dia ditawarin duit sama orang yang sekarang nyari Sekar."
  en: "This is Raka, Sekar's friend. Tasya knew Sekar was threatened a week before she disappeared, and said nothing. She was offered money by the people now looking for Sekar."
narration
  id: Semuanya bener. Dan semuanya salah.
  en: All of it true. And all of it wrong.

media CG cg_wrong_name.webp unlock=cg_wrong_name
  id: Dalam satu jam, screenshot-nya ada di mana-mana. Akun @carikaksekar nge-repost. Komentar-komentarnya nggak bisa dibaca sampai habis.
  en: Within an hour, the screenshot is everywhere. The @findkaksekar account reposts it. The comments can't be read to the end.

narration
  id: Paginya, akun Tasya hilang. Podcast-nya di-private. Dia nggak pernah ngangkat telepon Dinda lagi.
  en: In the morning, Tasya's accounts are gone. The podcast is set to private. She never picks up Dinda's calls again.
narration
  id: Bima berhenti bales chat. Didit nggak perlu ngelakuin apa-apa. Orang-orang yang dia takutin udah saling bubar sendiri.
  en: Bima stops replying. Didit doesn't have to do anything. The people he was afraid of have scattered on their own.
narration
  id: Dua minggu kemudian, gue balik ke Bandung. Kadang gue buka grup itu. Sepi. Pesan terakhir di sana masih punya gue.
  en: Two weeks later, I go back to Bandung. Sometimes I open that group. It's silent. The last message there is still mine.

ending end_08_wrong_name BAD
  id: Nama yang Salah
  en: Wrong Name
  summary id: Raka menuduh Tasya di depan semua pendengar. Kelompok kecil yang bisa menemukan Sekar bubar, dan orang yang sebenarnya tidak tersentuh.
  summary en: Raka accused Tasya in front of every listener. The small group that could have found Sekar fell apart, and the real culprit was never touched.


